\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Following the B19 methodology, I computed temporal correlation matrices from the physically consistent DP21 ensemble trajectories by calculating the correlation among the 2100, 2200, and 2300 projections. I generated both:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Scenario-specific matrices
\f1\b0  (RCP2.6, RCP4.5, RCP8.5), and\
\ls1\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A B19-style combined matrix
\f1\b0  by vertically concatenating the three scenario ensembles before calculating the correlations.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Across all components, temporal dependence is generally very strong, particularly between 
\f0\b 2200 and 2300
\f1\b0  (typically >0.97 for Total AIS and >0.88 for WAIS/EAIS). This suggests that ensemble member rankings are largely preserved over the later projection period.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The largest scenario dependence occurs for 
\f0\b WAIS
\f1\b0 . Under RCP8.5, the 2100\'962300 correlation drops to 
\f0\b 0.47
\f1\b0 , compared to 
\f0\b 0.81
\f1\b0  under RCP2.6 and 
\f0\b 0.78
\f1\b0  under RCP4.5, indicating substantially more rank reshuffling under stronger forcing. EAIS also shows weaker long-term correlations under higher forcing, although the effect is less pronounced. Total AIS is comparatively more stable because the EAIS contribution moderates the WAIS behavior.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 
\f0\b combined (B19-style) matrices
\f1\b0  generally produce higher correlations than the scenario-specific matrices. This is expected because pooling the scenarios captures both (1) temporal dependence within each scenario and (2) separation among scenarios, rather than only the within-scenario dependence.\
